The identity count falls because deduplication removed 97 of the 5,000
sampled grants as superseded filings, and because identities are grants
collapsed on normalized name+address, so the two do not fall in step.

Both `clear` columns above are YES over the RESULT FRAME -- these are
saved benchmark frames and the in-scope identity count is not in them, so
identities no pass retrieved for are missing from both numerator and
denominator. The decomposition separates the population move from the
matching move; it cannot recover the retrieval failures neither base
counts. For that, read a run through pf_result_tiers() against x$in_scope
(dev/bench-md-reference.R, dev/adjudicate-16-fuzzy-regress.R).
